0..77 Comment "// A buffer the ring allocates is live from its allocation until it is freed:"
78..154 Comment "// the kernel owns it while an operation is in flight and hands it back with"
155..232 Comment "// the completion (boats, _Notes on io-uring_, 2020), so the program holds it"
233..311 Comment "// exactly once at every step. `Buf` is the host\'s buffer, allocated and freed"
312..387 Comment "// through the `Ring` interface; a scope handling `Ring` serves the buffers"
388..462 Comment "// itself, minting each one its `alloc` clause resumes with and reclaiming"
463..502 Comment "// each one its `free` clause receives."
504..581 Comment "/// A buffer allocated and freed: the allocation places it live, and the free"
582..657 Comment "/// hands it back to the scope that minted it. The `alloc` clause lends its"
658..726 Comment "/// mint to a mock kernel, which fills it and hands it back with the"
727..777 Comment "/// completion, before the clause resumes with it."
